Link numpy's extensions as iOS dylibs instead of Mach-O bundles.

This patch is conditional and currently inert. meta.yaml applies it only when
`version < (2, 0)`, and the recipe builds a 2.x numpy, so it is never applied
and never reaches the source tree. It is kept for the case where the recipe is
pointed back at a 1.26.x version, where it is still required.

numpy 1.x vendors its own copy of meson under `vendored-meson/`, so the recipe
cannot get this fixed by upgrading the build backend — the vendored tree is
what runs. On Apple targets that meson links every Python extension module as
a Mach-O bundle (`-bundle`, filetype MH_BUNDLE), which is what CPython's own
loader expects on macOS. iOS does not accept it: the app's dynamic loader
refuses anything that is not MH_OBJECT or MH_DYLIB, so without this change
every numpy extension fails at import with "Unsupported mach-o filetype".
Linking with `-dynamiclib` instead produces MH_DYLIB and the extensions load.

For 2.x the patch is unnecessary because forge's own fix_wheel step rewrites
the filetype from MH_BUNDLE to MH_DYLIB after the build, for every recipe, so
the link flag no longer has to be right in the first place. If the patch is
ever revived, check that its single hunk still lands: it targets
`get_std_shared_module_args` on meson's Apple dynamic-linker class, and the
vendored meson tree moved between 1.x releases.

diff --git a/vendored-meson/meson/mesonbuild/linkers/linkers.py b/vendored-meson/meson/mesonbuild/linkers/linkers.py
index 7b3202c..2bf5e19 100644
--- a/vendored-meson/meson/mesonbuild/linkers/linkers.py
+++ b/vendored-meson/meson/mesonbuild/linkers/linkers.py
@@ -767,7 +767,7 @@ def get_allow_undefined_args(self) -> T.List[str]:
         return self._apply_prefix('-undefined,dynamic_lookup')
 
     def get_std_shared_module_args(self, options: 'KeyedOptionDictType') -> T.List[str]:
-        return ['-bundle'] + self._apply_prefix('-undefined,dynamic_lookup')
+        return ['-dynamiclib'] + self._apply_prefix('-undefined,dynamic_lookup')
 
     def get_pie_args(self) -> T.List[str]:
         return []
